Aim
To capture or open cellular network traces in Wireshark and analyse GSM, GTP, S1AP and NGAP signalling and user-plane messages.
Detailed Algorithm
1.  Install Wireshark (with tshark). Download public sample captures for GSM, GTP, S1AP and NGAP from the Wireshark Sample Captures wiki page (or use captures supplied by your lab).
2.  Open a capture and look at Statistics > Protocol Hierarchy to identify the protocols present.
3.  GSM: apply the filters gsm_a.dtap, gsm_a.bssmap, gsm_map or gsm_sms and list the call-control, mobility-management and SMS messages.
4.  GTP: apply gtp (GTPv1) or gtpv2; identify Create PDP Context or Create Session Request/Response and the G-PDU packets that carry user data inside the tunnel (note the TEID).
5.  S1AP (LTE): apply s1ap over SCTP; list the attach procedure messages (Initial UE Message, NAS messages, Initial Context Setup).
6.  NGAP (5G): apply ngap over SCTP; list the registration and PDU session messages.
7.  Export the message flow with Statistics > Flow Graph and take screenshots.
8.  Repeat the analysis with tshark from the command line to extract fields.
